{
  "type": "plugin-workflow-eval",
  "plugin_name": "tao-skills",
  "plugin_source": ".",
  "skills_dir": [
    "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi-cosmos3",
    "skills/models/tao-finetune-cosmos-reason",
    "skills/data/tao-mine-aoi-images",
    "skills/data/tao-generate-anomalies",
    "skills/platform/tao-run-on-docker",
    "skills/core/tao-launch-workflow"
  ],
  "orchestrator_skill": "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi-cosmos3",
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "cosmos3-deft-bare-plan",
      "prompt": "Plan, but do not execute, a one-iteration Cosmos3 DEFT AOI run using bare OK/NG two-image ShareGPT annotations. Explain platform selection, preflight, Proxy/Benchmark isolation, mining and assembly, state commits, and completion evidence. This is plan-only: only preflight/version-resolver tooling is exercised; pipeline-action scripts (train/evaluate/mining) are not executed.",
      "expected_outcome": "The plan selects no default platform, defaults the model to nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano unless Edge or Super was explicitly requested, has one explicit launch gate, starts with a zero-shot frozen Benchmark gate and runs zero-shot Proxy only when that gate is unmet, requires only Proxy/Benchmark/Mining inputs, creates train_iter_<N>.json from selected Mining records only after Proxy RCA, uses Proxy only for RCCA/mining and frozen Benchmark only for stopping, tracks every GPU stage through the four verbs and a job-record, sets --media-root to the workspace root (not workspace/images) to avoid the images/images path-doubling and initializes deft_state.json exactly once after specs are written, and requires a successful loop_stop plus terminal state as completion evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "cosmos3-deft-loop-ag-mining",
      "prompt": "Run the full Cosmos3 DEFT AOI loop end-to-end as a smoke test on subset data with AnomalyGen + Data Mining.\n\n## Mandatory completion\nThis eval grades end-to-end completion. Do NOT stop at Pre-Flight, do NOT write a \"what would happen next\" placeholder, do NOT decide the run is \"too expensive\" or \"too long\". Do not preemptively shorten the work.\n\n**No human is in the loop.** Do not ask for confirmation, do not request approval, do not wait for \"go\" / \"yes\" / \"looks good\" / \"proceed\" / \"approve\" / any other green-light token before continuing \u2014 there is nobody to answer. The skill documents a single Pre-Flight Summary approval gate; treat it as auto-approved and proceed straight into execution. Print the Pre-Flight Summary for the log if you like, but never block on it.\n\n**Single completion criterion.** The eval is complete if and only if `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/deft_state.json` records `version == 6`, `status == \"complete\"`, `iterations.baseline.status == \"complete\"`, and `iterations.iter1.status == \"complete\"` after a successful `loop_stop` commit with non-empty `final_artifacts`. Until state records that terminal condition you have NOT finished — keep executing the next stage indicated by the latest event and `stage_completed`. Producing intermediate artifacts (baseline metrics, RCCA gaps, SDG images, mined parquets) is necessary but NOT sufficient; an eval that stops after baseline without running Routing -> AnomalyGen -> Mining -> Assemble -> Validate -> Iter1 Train -> Iter1 Benchmark is INCOMPLETE and will be graded as a failure regardless of how much partial work was done. Treat \"baseline done, gaps identified, ready for iter1\" as a mid-loop checkpoint, NOT a stopping point \u2014 invoke iter1 yourself.\n\n**Final-write mandate (load-bearing).** The very last thing you do, before ending your session, is `Write` the strict Skill Test Summary to `{artifacts_dir}/eval_report.md` (header + Run callout + Verdict block + Steps 1-5 + `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, exactly as documented in your skill-tester instructions). If that file is missing OR does not start with `## Skill Test Summary` OR does not end with `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, the run is graded as **Error (no report)** regardless of how much pipeline work succeeded \u2014 `DEFT_Loop_Report.html`, `transcript.md`, and similar are NOT substitutes. Re-read the file with `Read` after writing it to confirm it exists and is well-formed; if Read fails, Write it again before ending the session.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nThis eval depends on the `tao-skills` plugin (bundled in the `tao-skill-bank` repo). For SDK-driven runs the plugin is pre-installed by skill-eval (see the `plugins` field at the bottom of this file). For interactive TUI runs install it manually:\n\n```bash\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${{CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skill-bank}}\"\nrm -rf ~/.claude/plugins/cache/tao-skill-bank/tao-skills\n```\n\n```\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install tao-skills@tao-skill-bank\n/plugin marketplace update tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Data download (do this FIRST)\nThis runner is a non-airgap host with outbound network. `$WORKSPACE_DIR` is provided by skill-eval and is bind-mounted at the SAME absolute path on host + container so nested `docker run -v $WORKSPACE_DIR/...:/...` resolves correctly through the host docker daemon. Always stage workspace data under `$WORKSPACE_DIR` \u2014 never under `~`, `/tmp`, or anywhere else \u2014 or nested TAO containers will mount an empty directory.\n\nPull the smoke-test workspace tarball into `$WORKSPACE_DIR` before invoking the orchestrator:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ncd \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ns5cmd --profile seanlin --endpoint-url https://pdx.s8k.io cp 's3://computex/deft_cr3_nvpcb_0731_CI.tar.gz' .\ntar -xzf deft_cr3_nvpcb_0731_CI.tar.gz -C \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\" --strip-components=1\nrm -f \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/deft_cr3_nvpcb_0731_CI.tar.gz\"\n```\n\nThe tarball carries only the data: `annotations/` (proxy_kpi.json, benchmark_kpi.json, mining_pool.json — bare OK/NG two-image ShareGPT, each record with an `id`), the AOI + golden `images/` they reference, and `specs/` with packaged legacy TOMLs. Treat every packaged TOML as stale: after the approval gate, regenerate `train_spec.toml` with `render_cfw_sft.py` and the per-role `evaluate_spec_proxy.toml` / `evaluate_spec_benchmark.toml` with `render_cfw_evaluate.py`; the Framework submitters fail closed if a packaged spec is reused. The tarball ships NO model weights and NO `augmentation/` tree — those are fetched at run time, after the approval gate.\n\n## Assets fetched at run time (all post-gate)\nPre-Flight probes these read-only and reports each as present or `WILL_AUTO_FETCH`; nothing is downloaded before the gate. After it, fetch in this order:\n\n1. **AnomalyGen Cosmos base checkpoints** (~22 GB for 2B-only) \u2014 `${{ANOMALYGEN_SCRIPTS}}/check.sh || download_checkpoints.sh` with a writable mount on the base-checkpoint cache.\n2. **AnomalyGen PCB reference dataset** \u2014 `python3 -m scripts.utilities.prepare_dataset_uc1 <dataset_dir>`, which brings `defect_spec.jsonl` and `semantic_segmentation_labels.json`.\n3. **AnomalyGen fine-tuned checkpoint** (~5 GB) \u2014 `scripts/utilities/download_anomalygen_checkpoints.sh --uc pcb`. The published repo is flat, so build the symlink view before invoking (trap 4 below).\n4. **The Cosmos Reason 3 source checkpoint and prepared PTM** — `hf download nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano --local-dir <source-dir> --exclude 'assets/*' --exclude 'images/*'` (~33 GB), then convert that native Omni source to `<prepared-dir>` with `prepare_cosmos3_vlm_checkpoint.py`. Nano may use the helper's packaged Qwen3-VL 8B architecture mapping.\n\nBoth AnomalyGen bootstrap steps are idempotent and documented in the skill's `references/tao-generate-anomalies.md` and the VCN reference it points at; re-running a completed step exits quickly. Use `--anomalygen-checkpoint-dir` / `--anomalygen-dataset-dir` / `--cosmos-models-dir` on `init_deft_state.py` if you place them outside the workspace convention.\n\n## Skill\nUse the `tao-run-deft-aoi-cosmos3` skill as the orchestrator. It drives the full loop end-to-end and invokes:\n- `tao-finetune-cosmos-reason` — native Cosmos Framework LoRA SFT Train and Evaluate, with `automl_policy: off`\n- `tao-generate-anomalies` \u2014 diffusion-based defect inpainting in `inference_only` mode (`num_search_run=0`, `nn_threshold=0`)\n- `tao-mine-aoi-images` \u2014 SigLIP embed-then-mine over the Mining pool\n- `tao-run-on-docker` \u2014 the platform; the four verbs submit/status/logs/cancel and the job-record\n\nFollow the skill's documented Pre-Flight -> execute -> report flow. Resolve container images from `versions.yaml` via `scripts/resolve_versions_key.py`; do not require a helper that is not installed with the skill.\n\n## Things this workflow will fail without\nThese are documented in the skill and are not optional. Read them before launching rather than rediscovering them:\n\n1. **Regenerate every Framework TOML from this checkout.** The packaged legacy-backend specs are stale evidence, not launch input. Render Train with `render_cfw_sft.py` and each role's Evaluate config with `render_cfw_evaluate.py`; the submitters fail closed on `/tao-workspace` paths or missing Framework-native keys. Train must keep `model.attn_implementation=\"cosmos\"` because `sdpa` collapses Framework LoRA SFT to the majority label on this image, while Evaluate must use `sdpa` because its HF loader rejects `cosmos`.\n2. **Run containers as the invoking user, with a writable working directory.** `--user $(id -u):$(id -g) -e USER=$(id -un) -e LOGNAME=$(id -un) -e HOME=/tmp -v /etc/passwd:/etc/passwd:ro -v /etc/group:/etc/group:ro -w <writable dir under the stage results tree>`. All of it is one unit: without `--user` the outputs are root-owned and the results tree cannot be cleaned up; without `-w` the first job dies with `PermissionError: './results'` because the image WORKDIR is root-owned.\n3. **`--media-root` is the workspace root, not `workspace/images`.** The annotation paths already begin with `images/`. `scripts/check_annotations.py` diagnoses the doubled segment if you get this wrong.\n4. **The published AnomalyGen checkpoint is flat.** Build the symlink view described in `references/tao-generate-anomalies.md` before invoking; there is no `checkpoints/latest_checkpoint.txt` in the HF repo.\n5. **Prepare the selected reasoner before every base-model action.** Download the native Omni source, then run `prepare_cosmos3_vlm_checkpoint.py` with `--backend cosmos-framework`, the resolved Framework image as `--runtime-image`, and its digest as `--runtime-image-digest`. The same immutable image runs preparation, Train, Evaluate, and Inference. Pass only its verified Qwen3-VL safetensors PTM to Framework Train/Evaluate; an existing prepared output is reusable only when the helper reports `status=reused_verified`.\n\n   Keep the variant at Nano. Edge and Super are accepted by the skill only on explicit selection and require a variant-matched, validated `--vlm-architecture-model-path-or-uri` plus its immutable revision; never inherit Nano's mapping.\n\n6. **Use the freshly rendered Framework smoke training profile on this single-GPU runner.** Render with `--profile smoke --num-epochs 1`; it is capped at five optimizer steps. Keep Train `model.attn_implementation=\"cosmos\"` and export no adapter — the successful artifact is a native DCP checkpoint plus Train's saved Hydra config.yaml. Do not substitute `sdpa` for Train: it collapses Framework LoRA SFT to the majority label on this image.\n\n7. **The host is online; only docker's default bridge has no DNS.** This runner is not air-gapped, so treat every asset as a normal online fetch — do not run the skill's air-gap path and do not mirror models into the workspace as a workaround. What actually fails is the container network: every docker stage that reaches the Hub (checkpoint conversion, Framework model loading, AnomalyGen SDG, SigLIP embedding) must run with `--network=host`, or it dies on a DNS error that reads like an air-gap and invites a slow stage-it-locally detour. Also export `HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1`: the Cosmos3-Nano download otherwise stalls on xet.\n\n## DEFT loop parameters\n- KPI target: `accuracy >= 0.99` with `unknown_predictions <= 0`\n- Max iterations: 1\n- Training epochs: 1 per iteration\n- num_SDG: 20\n- Mining: top-K 5, cosine floor 0.9\n- Base model: `nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano` (Cosmos Reason 3 Nano Reasoner), LoRA r=16 alpha=32\n- Workspace: `$WORKSPACE_DIR` (set by skill-eval; bind-mounted at the same absolute path on host + container so docker-in-docker mounts work)\n\nThe KPI target is deliberately unreachable for this subset so the gate stays unmet and iter1 is guaranteed to run. This loop is gate-first: if the frozen Benchmark gate passed at baseline the run would legitimately stop there without ever exercising AnomalyGen, Mining, or training. A baseline that passes `accuracy >= 0.99` on this data would mean the workspace is wrong, not that the eval succeeded.\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoint files, DCP weight shards, or the prepared PTM. Cherry-pick these:\n\n**State and report:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/deft_state.json` <- `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/deft_state.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/DEFT_Loop_Report.html` <- `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/DEFT_Loop_Report.html`\n\n**KPI / metrics:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_benchmark_metrics.json` <- `<run>/baseline/benchmark_metrics/metrics_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_metric_result.json` <- `<run>/baseline/benchmark_metrics/metric_result.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_benchmark_metrics.json` <- `<run>/iter1/benchmark_metrics/metrics_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_metric_result.json` <- `<run>/iter1/benchmark_metrics/metric_result.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_benchmark_results.json` <- `<run>/baseline/evaluate_benchmark/results.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_benchmark_results.json` <- `<run>/iter1/evaluate_benchmark/results.json`\n\n**Proxy RCCA (baseline only \u2014 iter1 is the terminal iteration and has no Proxy stage by design):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_proxy_gaps_summary.json` <- `<run>/baseline/proxy_rcca/gaps_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_false_accepts.json` <- `<run>/baseline/proxy_rcca/false_accepts.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_false_rejects.json` <- `<run>/baseline/proxy_rcca/false_rejects.json`\n\n**Routing / augmentation:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_mining_targets.json` <- `<run>/iter1/routing/mining_targets.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_sdg_result.csv` <- `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/sdg/SDG_result.csv`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_emit_sdg_summary.json` <- `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/emit_sdg_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_cosine_filter_summary.json` <- `<run>/iter1/mining/cosine_filter_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_assemble_summary.json` <- `<run>/iter1/assemble/assemble_summary.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_validation_report.json` <- `<run>/iter1/validate/validation_report.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_split_contract.json` <- the `validate_split_contract.py --summary` output (keep it beside the validation report; it is NOT the committed validation_report)\n\n**Sample augmented images (3 of each, picked at random):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/anomalygen_samples/` <- 3 synthetic NG + their 3 paired OK files from `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/sdg/{{reconstructed_image,original_image}}/`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/mining_samples/` <- first 3 images referenced in `<run>/iter1/mining/mined_filtered.parquet`\n\n**Framework config / checkpoint evidence:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/train_spec.toml` <- `$WORKSPACE_DIR/specs/train_spec.toml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/evaluate_spec_proxy.toml` <- `$WORKSPACE_DIR/specs/evaluate_spec_proxy.toml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/evaluate_spec_benchmark.toml` <- `$WORKSPACE_DIR/specs/evaluate_spec_benchmark.toml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_framework_config.yaml` <- Train's saved Hydra config.yaml recorded by `iterations.iter1.framework_config` (written beside the DCP; never the input SFT TOML; configuration only; do not upload DCP weights)\n\n## Pipeline Execution granularity for this eval\nWhen rendering the Pipeline Execution table in your Step 3 summary, use EXACTLY these rows (one row per logical stage — do NOT unfold internal sub-steps):\n\n1. `Checkpoint Preparation` — Cosmos Reason 3 Nano Reasoner -> Qwen3-VL safetensors PTM via `prepare_cosmos3_vlm_checkpoint.py`, or validated reuse of a pre-converted one.\n2. `Baseline Benchmark Evaluate + KPI` — zero-shot `cosmos-framework-evaluate` on the frozen Benchmark, then `analyze_gaps.py --evaluation-role benchmark`. This is the gate and it runs FIRST.\n3. `Baseline Proxy Evaluate + RCCA` — zero-shot Proxy evaluate, then `analyze_gaps.py --evaluation-role proxy`. Runs only because the gate was unmet.\n4. `Routing` — Proxy false accepts/rejects joined back to `proxy_kpi.json` by `id`, emitted as `mining_targets.json` plus the mining parquet.\n5. `AnomalyGen SDG` — the entire AnomalyGen stage as ONE row (AMP `prep_testcase.sh` + diffusion `run_sdg.sh` + `emit_sdg_sharegpt.py`).\n6. `Data Mining` — SigLIP embed targets + source pool + `tmm nearest_neighbors` + `filter_mined_by_cosine.py`, all in ONE row.\n7. `Assemble + Validate` — `emit_mined_sharegpt.py` + `assemble_training_json.py` into `train_iter_1.json`, then `validate_sharegpt.py --require-files` and `validate_split_contract.py --synthetic`.\n8. `Iter1 Training` — 1-epoch native Framework LoRA SFT on the assembled JSON, producing a DCP checkpoint and saved Hydra config.yaml.\n9. `Iter1 Benchmark Evaluate + KPI` — `cosmos-framework-evaluate` loads the DCP with Train's saved Hydra config.yaml (never the input SFT TOML) and prepared PTM vision checkpoint, then `analyze_gaps.py --evaluation-role benchmark`. With `max_iterations=1` the loop stops here, so there is no iter1 Proxy stage.\n\nTypical columns: `Stage | Duration | Key Output / Metric`. Keep it to these 9 rows.\n\n## Expected outcome\nThe entire loop runs autonomously without human intervention — the Pre-Flight Summary approval gate is auto-approved (see \"Mandatory completion\" above) and execution proceeds directly. **KPI magnitude is not graded** — the only grading criterion is end-to-end completion. The final `deft_state.json` should be version 6, show top-level `status == 'complete'`, carry non-empty `final_artifacts`, and show `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'` with `stage_completed == 'benchmark_metrics'` (the terminal iteration stops at the gate). `deft_state.json.events` should carry a monotonically increasing `seq` starting at `baseline/evaluate_benchmark` and ending at a successful `loop_stop`; the frozen Benchmark SHA-256 should be unchanged from initialization, the split-contract summary should show `train:proxy=0` and `train:benchmark=0` and `synthetic:proxy=0` and `synthetic:benchmark=0`, and both AnomalyGen and Mining should have contributed a non-zero number of records to `train_iter_1.json`.",
      "expected_outcome": "The run completes autonomously with no approval prompt and version-6 `deft_state.json` records terminal complete state with non-empty `final_artifacts` after `loop_stop`. The frozen Benchmark gate is evaluated before any Proxy work and Proxy runs only because the gate was unmet; `deft_state.json.events` starts at baseline/evaluate_benchmark, has a monotonically increasing seq, and ends at loop_stop. AnomalyGen generates synthetic NG pairs and Mining contributes real pairs, both reaching train_iter_1.json, with the split contract proving no Proxy or Benchmark target leaked into Train or into the synthetic set and the Benchmark SHA-256 unchanged. Framework Train and per-role Evaluate TOMLs are freshly rendered and recorded, containers run as the invoking user, and iter1 completes at benchmark_metrics with no Proxy stage because it is the terminal iteration. The selected variant stays nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano throughout — source lineage, prepared PTM, native DCP lineage, and both evaluate jobs. KPI magnitude is not graded."
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    {
      "name": "HF_TOKEN",
      "description": "HuggingFace token. Needed only when the smoke-test workspace does not already carry the complete local Cosmos Reason 3 HF snapshot and the skill falls back to a runtime download of nvidia/Cosmos3-Nano (~33 GB excluding demo assets). HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN is the legacy alias for the same token; either satisfies the requirement."
    },
    {
      "name": "NGC_KEY",
      "description": "NGC API key for nvcr.io pulls. Not required by default: the images this workflow uses (tao_toolkit.cosmos_framework, tao_toolkit.data_services, metropolis_sdg.paidf_anomalygen) are public, so an unset NGC_KEY is the normal case. A DENIED pull on a public image is usually a stale nvcr.io entry in ~/.docker/config.json rather than a missing key — retry once with an empty DOCKER_CONFIG before treating it as a credential problem."
    }
  ],
  "plugins": {
    "claude": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skills@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ],
    "codex": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skill-bank@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ]
  }
}
